.SH "NAME"
nvme-ocp-set-latency-monitor-feature \- Set Latency Monitor Feature
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIocp set\-latency\-monitor\-feature\fR <device>
                        [\-\-active_bucket_timer_threshold=<num> | \-t <num>]
                        [\-\-active_threshold_a=<num> | \-a <num>]
                        [\-\-active_threshold_b=<num> | \-b <num>]
                        [\-\-active_threshold_c=<num> | \-c <num>]
                        [\-\-active_threshold_d=<num> | \-d <num>]
                        [\-\-active_latency_config=<num> | \-f <num>]
                        [\-\-active_latency_minimum_window=<num> | \-w <num>]
                        [\-\-debug_log_trigger_enable=<num> | \-r <num>]
                        [\-\-discard_debug_log=<num> | \-l <num>]
                        [\-\-latency_monitor_feature_enable=<num> | \-e <num>]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Set Latency Monitor Feature\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and may be either the NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0), or a namespace block device (ex: /dev/nvme0n1)\&.
.sp
This page only lists the help texts of the command\&. A detailed description is still missing\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-t <num>, \-\-active_bucket_timer_threshold=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads the Active Bucket Timer Threshold\&.
.RE
.PP
\-a <num>, \-\-active_threshold_a=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Active Threshold A\&.
.RE
.PP
\-b <num>, \-\-active_threshold_b=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Active Threshold B\&.
.RE
.PP
\-c <num>, \-\-active_threshold_c=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Active Threshold C\&.
.RE
.PP
\-d <num>, \-\-active_threshold_d=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Active Threshold D\&.
.RE
.PP
\-f <num>, \-\-active_latency_config=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Active Latency Configuration\&.
.RE
.PP
\-w <num>, \-\-active_latency_minimum_window=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Active Latency Minimum Window\&.
.RE
.PP
\-r <num>, \-\-debug_log_trigger_enable=<num>
.RS 4
This is the value that loads into the Debug Log Trigger Enable\&.
.RE
.PP
\-l <num>, \-\-discard_debug_log=<num>
.RS 4
Discard Debug Log\&.
.RE
.PP
\-e <num>, \-\-latency_monitor_feature_enable=<num>
.RS 4
Latency Monitor Feature Enable\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&. Other versions are rejected\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-quiet
.RS 4
Suppress informational messages\&. Errors are still reported, and \-\-quiet cancels any \-\-verbose for the library log level\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-set\-options=<key=value>[,<key=value>\&...]
.RS 4
Set libnvme library options for this invocation\&. Supported keys are
\fIforce\-4k\fR,
\fImi\-probe\-enabled\fR,
\fItest\-base\-dir\fR
and
\fItest\-sysfs\-dir\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
\fIinfinite\fR
or
\fI\-1\fR
waits without a time limit (0xffffffff)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
